INSERT INTO drafts ("id", "window_id", "cluster_id", "channel", "prompt_version", "content", "content_hash", "source_event_ids", "status", "reviewed_by", "review_notes", "approved_at", "created_at", "updated_at", "guardrail_score", "guardrail_passed", "guardrail_reasons", "llm_model", "reviewer_id", "reviewer_note", "reviewed_at", "generated_at") VALUES ('5311b97a6a20513eb23c5a6c15583bb0'::uuid, '20260623T1325_20261005T1725', '20260623T1325_20261005T1725_c1', 'LINKEDIN', 'v2', 'SSH remains the primary standard for remote access, yet many engineers struggle with the specific syntax required for advanced networking tasks like reverse tunneling. Whether you are studying for the CompTIA A+ Core 1 (220-1101) exam or debugging a production server, understanding how TCP port 22 handles traffic is a fundamental requirement for systems administration. While most users stop at basic shell access, the OpenSSH protocol provides the infrastructure to bypass NAT or expose local development servers to the public internet without a dedicated VPN.

- Use ssh -R to open a listening port on a remote server that pipes traffic back to your local machine, a process that often requires enabling GatewayPorts in the sshd_config to allow external traffic.
- Replace unencrypted legacy protocols like Telnet (port 23) and FTP (ports 20 and 21) with SSH-based alternatives to ensure all terminal and file transfer data remains encrypted.
- Manage identity and security during the connection handshake by using the -l flag for specific usernames and rigorously verifying host key fingerprints on the first connection.

Mastering the technical distinction between local and remote port forwarding transforms a simple command-line client into a versatile tool for modern network troubleshooting.

How often do you rely on SSH reverse tunnels instead of traditional VPNs when testing webhooks on a local dev server?', '5121424ca3929ddd46a29e82a886dc45f8aae731625f0b0b67f2b2d3e0b8b64b', '{9a5d100a21e947dab78a90eed77b992e,d45ac8deb03b4713a75c61abd5fecd9d,cd7dc6fe62424bdebc2827c107bf7bd5}'::uuid[]::uuid[], 'IN_REVIEW', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-05 17:25:22.412045+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-10-05 17:52:48.300009+00:00'::timestamptz, 1.0, true, '{}'::jsonb, 'gemini-3-flash-preview', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-05 17:27:05.072533+00:00'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO drafts ("id", "window_id", "cluster_id", "channel", "prompt_version", "content", "content_hash", "source_event_ids", "status", "reviewed_by", "review_notes", "approved_at", "created_at", "updated_at", "guardrail_score", "guardrail_passed", "guardrail_reasons", "llm_model", "reviewer_id", "reviewer_note", "reviewed_at", "generated_at") VALUES ('1ebf035ead4d54f4ad42898df8c1511d'::uuid, '20260623T1351_20261005T1751', '20260623T1351_20261005T1751_c1', 'LINKEDIN', 'v2', 'SSH isn’t just about secure logins—it can expose local services to the internet without a VPN.  
When a developer runs a test server on a laptop behind NAT, the only way to let a colleague on a remote host hit that service is to create a reverse tunnel: `ssh -R 8080:localhost:8080 user@remote.example.com`. The tunnel opens a listening port on the remote server and forwards any traffic back to the laptop, eliminating the need for port forwarding or a public IP.  

CompTIA A+ Core 1 (220‑1101) exam candidates also need to recall key port numbers:  
- FTP data and control use ports 20 and 21;  
- SSH and SFTP operate on port 22;  
- Telnet falls back to port 23, while SMTP uses port 25.  
A quick reference table locks these numbers in and helps troubleshoot firewall rules.  

What changed in practice:  
• `ssh -l sam example.com` lets you override the default local username without adding `user@`.  
• A changed host‑key fingerprint on a known host must be verified through a trusted channel—don’t ignore the prompt.  
• The `ssh -R` option now supports `GatewayPorts=yes` to allow remote clients to connect directly to the forwarded port.  

Lesson: Mastering SSH syntax and port conventions cuts configuration time and hardens security.  

How do you currently handle remote access to services behind NAT?', 'a989e3eeaabc486c7e9f87b72d8683befc33b9a920d267d6f8e82c92be76d98d', '{9a5d100a21e947dab78a90eed77b992e,d45ac8deb03b4713a75c61abd5fecd9d,cd7dc6fe62424bdebc2827c107bf7bd5}'::uuid[]::uuid[], 'IN_REVIEW', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-05 17:52:49.130160+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-10-05 17:52:50.985356+00:00'::timestamptz, 1.0, true, '{}'::jsonb, 'openai/gpt-oss-20b', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-05 17:52:50.974831+00:00'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO drafts ("id", "window_id", "cluster_id", "channel", "prompt_version", "content", "content_hash", "source_event_ids", "status", "reviewed_by", "review_notes", "approved_at", "created_at", "updated_at", "guardrail_score", "guardrail_passed", "guardrail_reasons", "llm_model", "reviewer_id", "reviewer_note", "reviewed_at", "generated_at") VALUES ('078ab333ce225a708e0cf24a8010ac57'::uuid, '20260623T1351_20261005T1751', '20260623T1351_20261005T1751_c0', 'LINKEDIN', 'v2', 'When an AI buyer agent pays its sellers, the proof must live on the blockchain, not in screenshots.  

On 3 October 2026 a builder posted a demo of an AI buyer agent that hired two sellers, paid only the one whose answer verified, and left the liar unpaid. I pulled the on‑chain receipts myself, querying BaseScan via Blockscout’s API, instead of relying on screenshots. Every transaction returned status ok, and the honest seller received 0.95 USDC, the hub signer 0.05 USDC, while the cheating seller received nothing. The settlementChannel transaction **0x11b02d8f…9b08** moved exactly these amounts out of escrow on Base mainnet.  

- Verified settlementChannel **0x11b02d8f…9b08** on BaseScan.  
- Honest seller **0x097e3F33…475a** received 0.95 USDC, hub signer **0xBE0bBE44…C5f1** got 0.05 USDC.  
- Cheating seller saw no payout, confirming audit integrity.  

Claims about agent money must be backed by on‑chain receipts, not screenshots.  

How do you ensure transparency in autonomous agent transactions in your projects?', 'bef386d214848ad1c8819e60c6ee348889f4314b96d07b7ca534cd619663ce89', '{0903d1e926d74254a9df675a2ac259e0,a68c6111073d4193975549866d752b09,6d57f7409b4e4c73901f2824c252f897,b8f315a21ef84e749bbedeff03751782,a731ef486dec40a7a7c181cb9264e0b6,ace21e67b0384bbc840bb20366d12953,3ed1c4a515514becadd482e9bea2cb8f,2066c8aa69f546b2a148e7d7bc4bdb98,f5b7f1912faa4ca0a1f8c1bf3e1ad23a,fc41fc64ef244b5daec6e3452d10dd6e,584f2f72c9e540fb98a2dc37739b8bd4,dff17fc8cc604e92a75a873bf8132469,6ac696a531034c02a20234f98119da94,9e275e3c6fcd4279b196265516840be2,8e34f69f88b9418c80bdb445ecaea529,b4dd31556d5041d0aaa06b68fd1c833b,f38a40393a754be2a54564cf7506cf2b,e95aac74f29b424bbd0035f00307dcd4,c2bb3c96f39644ca93cc1ed99023d0c7,c1a0b7f2b06d401e8bc243ade87685ba,5b1be25c4a0a4da59e9767a6782d122a,bffb6a7fbfc4407cbb6154854d2d3476,50ec5f146ba14e2eb790c661c90193be,cbe27c889cc34bcbb3bd30e3eaf6b213,9007a44e82fb4ecebb440b8a61515f57,27f12ab7fecb48638ba22693ab6c18e1,3739dfdf405448bcabb3e28a1a534ff8,2454dd1748a44f619af4653e9aa45750,3a49ea7d7d2b4f59a9682aaaba2e4d83,5dac438f285a4d859070f558b4ba5f9a,4cc5cf9799224ad7a6c91efa6e9e3e01,6f0d317a99e6415198e8d1f17ecca34f,1d7003b1098d46f0aaa0ee125a3056a6,c13b20589434424ab4ef55dd692daaf8,aece687eca82474abcaa14dde1a384e3,bf15d3f1e8614750b23d62f4fba7841e,bb8919be3c3b4c38b2418d3daefec439,37a657d63f7d41138bc665692bf84c0b,eaaa837a52bd43629345817a9af321b0,7c678f58ed1f4c1e911e3ed5b7e8f922,3f17c4257da24db09a4b16ce3cdd9d6f,013cb7837fdf43cbad9ce59800b9b9e4,43f0724a93b7490088fc3eeb0d9769df,3b79ebcc42cb486ab4ccf27dd84534d8,12c8e152d2224766bdad3bff31ded29c,bc5a84cbc7b141c08b0ac62c68795bfa,54726d8b193c489da51e3406f1b0b027,1872d87e10ff49cdb1f97e3421ea110d,32e8ef25263c43f382c73155f500f822,e358f7a826994e73827e3ecb1f27dbbd,1a204c8d0c444952b1bdd2f15f3f8f91,c3bda0b73e1b4fb2b4d7573d5a00ec51,737304e5986e44eca7d1ff6909f73791,2093fb43fc534ec095866b3edfe6e973,d121c53f67b0433ebfcca5368522de9c,2cfa3ede9f0747abababa76645bebfb