The platform, launched by Sam Bankman‑Fried in 2017, evaporated overnight, wiping out more than $8 billion of client balances and shattering confidence in the CEX model. Investigations traced the failure to structural gaps in asset custody, opaque governance, and a lack of independent audit trails—issues that had been hidden behind the promise of liquidity and convenience. The fallout has forced regulators to mandate stricter KYC and audit regimes for exchanges, while the broader tech community has turned its attention to seemingly unrelated misconfigurations, such as duplicate SPF records that trigger permerrors under RFC 7208, and the rapid decline of manual coding practices highlighted by DHH’s 2025 retirement from hand‑coding after the release of Opus 4.5.  

What changed  
- Centralized exchanges now must publish quarterly independent audit reports and maintain real‑time asset ledger visibility.  
- SPF policies must be merged into a single v=spf1 record; duplicate include statements are prohibited by RFC 7208 and cause permerror failures.  
- Developers are adopting agent‑based code generators and Rust back‑ends to eliminate manual code errors, a shift echoed by DHH’s move away from hand‑coding.  

Reliance on convenience without transparent governance creates systemic risk that can collapse entire ecosystems.  

What concrete steps will your organization take to ensure that ease of use does not compromise security and accountability in digital asset management?', '707bccce4e783c479949891a1c325c7b9f4d51c5ddd31c8db296207d3bbbf14d', '{e54ddd2d926a4616a638d8652e9b30ca,d355b1e3770b4fb4b88c9911d7ce0e9f,7a5f5a93458946c4bbf239ababbfa122}'::uuid[]::uuid[], 'IN_REVIEW', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-06 00:10:58.381441+00:00'::timestamptz, '2026-10-06 13:29:18.164177+00:00'::timestamptz, 1.0, true, '{}'::jsonb, 'openai/gpt-oss-20b', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-06 02:48:19.139559+00:00'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
