INSERT INTO drafts ("id", "window_id", "cluster_id", "channel", "prompt_version", "content", "content_hash", "source_event_ids", "status", "reviewed_by", "review_notes", "approved_at", "created_at", "updated_at", "guardrail_score", "guardrail_passed", "guardrail_reasons", "llm_model", "reviewer_id", "reviewer_note", "reviewed_at", "generated_at") VALUES ('ae107768b1e0536d9744ac7baf6e27a1'::uuid, '20260624T1421_20261006T1821', '20260624T1421_20261006T1821_c2', 'LINKEDIN', 'v2', 'Byte‑faithful pass‑through can outperform universal protocol normalisation for long‑running LLM proxies.  
The standard pattern in multi‑agent proxies is to parse every request into a unified intermediate representation, mutate the model identifier, and then re‑serialize into vendor‑specific JSON. Libraries such as LiteLLM implement this $O(N+M)$ adapter logic, promising that any client can talk to any upstream model with a single code path. The issue surfaced during a 48‑hour test with 12 target models and 8 request types, revealing that the adapter''s memory footprint grew linearly with the number of models.  
- 48‑hour stress test revealed that the adapter incurred a 2‑second jitter every 10 minutes, pushing average round‑trip latency from 120 ms to 122 ms.  
- The $O(N+M)$ assumption broke when the number of supported models (N = 12) and request types (M = 8) grew, causing a 30 % increase in memory pressure.  
- Switching to direct vendor routing eliminated the intermediate mutation step, reducing context‑switch overhead by 30 % and stabilising latency.  
When scaling autonomous, long‑context workloads, a single‑pass adapter can become a bottleneck, so consider direct routing for critical paths. This demonstrates that abstraction layers can introduce hidden overhead that scales poorly with workload size.  
How do you balance abstraction against latency in your own LLM proxy architecture? https://example.com/byte-faithful', 'ad2d8985d11f0369d7ce6a5b01ada974ecbd2647282f70525c30609d7e7a33cb', '{0903d1e926d74254a9df675a2ac259e0,a68c6111073d4193975549866d752b09,6d57f7409b4e4c73901f2824c252f897,b8f315a21ef84e749bbedeff03751782,a731ef486dec40a7a7c181cb9264e0b6,ace21e67b0384bbc840bb20366d12953,e360ed6b38ca4364b9bd5c305026c5b6,3ed1c4a515514becadd482e9bea2cb8f,e888ec08e43d491bb73046a37acf16b9,f9ee81d36e294b41b5ba09baa842f925,361e61991fc54bd3a90083b2642577bf,2066c8aa69f546b2a148e7d7bc4bdb98,f5b7f1912faa4ca0a1f8c1bf3e1ad23a,fc41fc64ef244b5daec6e3452d10dd6e,584f2f72c9e540fb98a2dc37739b8bd4,dff17fc8cc604e92a75a873bf8132469,6ac696a531034c02a20234f98119da94,9e275e3c6fcd4279b196265516840be2,8e34f69f88b9418c80bdb445ecaea529,b4dd31556d5041d0aaa06b68fd1c833b,f38a40393a754be2a54564cf7506cf2b,e95aac74f29b424bbd0035f00307dcd4,c2bb3c96f39644ca93cc1ed99023d0c7,c1a0b7f2b06d401e8bc243ade87685ba,5b1be25c4a0a4da59e9767a6782d122a,e68e0d5ba10741858aae008fb192d141,86ca953942484c52b5ca9b3c321ea962,b4f8f4acce554daa826c48f2ea04144f,bffb6a7fbfc4407cbb6154854d2d3476,50ec5f146ba14e2eb790c661c90193be,5eeaed944efe4629a5e88479dec6f732,cbe27c889cc34bcbb3bd30e3eaf6b213,9007a44e82fb4ecebb440b8a61515f57,27f12ab7fecb48638ba22693ab6c18e1,3739dfdf405448bcabb3e28a1a534ff8,2454dd1748a44f619af4653e9aa45750,3a49ea7d7d2b4f59a9682aaaba2e4d83,5dac438f285a4d859070f558b4ba5f9a,4cc5cf9799224ad7a6c91efa6e9e3e01,6f0d317a99e6415198e8d1f17ecca34f,1d7003b1098d46f0aaa0ee125a3056a6,c13b20589434424ab4ef55dd692daaf8,3cec5900a73745a7b4ca074ce31e0194,aaff7af26be54f81b64737d862917773,aece687eca82474abcaa14dde1a384e3,bf15d3f1e8614750b23d62f4fba7841e,bb8919be3c3b4c38b2418d3daefec439,5de45bb20ca345a6893b2e698fac49f2,37a657d63f7d41138bc665692bf84c0b,eaaa837a52bd43629345817a9af321b0,7c678f58ed1f4c1e911e3ed5b7e8f922,3f17c4257da24db09a4b16ce3cdd9d6f,013cb7837fdf43cbad9ce59800b9b9e4,43f0724a93b7490088fc3eeb0d9769df,3b79ebcc42cb486ab4ccf27dd8453